system "Shared counter"

# Two workers each add one to a shared counter by reading it, then writing
# back what they read plus one. Nothing stops them from interleaving.

types
  worker is one of alice, bob
  phase is one of idle, holding, done

state
  counter is an integer from 0 to 2
  seen is a map from worker to an integer from 0 to 2
  at is a map from worker to phase

initially
  counter is 0
  seen of every worker is 0
  at of every worker is idle

always
  (every w in worker satisfies at of w is done) implies counter is 2

action read(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is idle
  seen of w becomes counter
  at of w becomes holding

action write(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is holding
  counter becomes seen of w + 1
  at of w becomes done
